# Line endings.
#
# Windows ends a line with two invisible characters (CRLF), macOS and Linux with
# one (LF). A team that mixes the two gets files that look "changed" when nobody
# touched them. This line makes Git store and check out text files with LF on
# every computer.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows command scripts are the exception: they need CRLF to run.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary files. Git must never try to change line endings inside these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
